WEBVTT

00:00:00.430 --> 00:00:05.950
In the name of the Father and of the Son and of the Holy Spirit, Amen.

00:00:05.950 --> 00:00:14.430
The reading from the Sinhaxadeon for September 15th, on which we commemorate, Saint Simeon

00:00:14.430 --> 00:00:18.860
Archbishop of Thessalonica.

00:00:18.860 --> 00:00:23.300
Our Holy Father Simeon was from Constantinople.

00:00:23.300 --> 00:00:30.700
After completing his education in secular learning and divinity, he cultivated the virtues

00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:42.140
of the angelic life, humility, meekness, self-control, and prayer, before succeeding Gabriel

00:00:42.140 --> 00:00:52.020
who died in the year 1416, or 1418, on the Episcopal throne of Thessalonica.

00:00:52.020 --> 00:00:58.660
In those difficult days, when the capital of Macedonia was about to pass under the Turkish

00:00:58.660 --> 00:01:04.020
yoke, Simeon proved an incomparable shepherd.

00:01:04.020 --> 00:01:11.660
In spite of poor health and frequent illness, he fed his flock unfailingly with the honey

00:01:11.660 --> 00:01:18.700
of his words, renewing their courage in the difficulties that beset them, and exhorting

00:01:18.700 --> 00:01:22.820
them to place all their hope in God.

00:01:22.820 --> 00:01:28.780
He had great trials to endure from those who were tempted to surrender the city, either

00:01:28.780 --> 00:01:32.820
to the Turks or the Venetians.

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:39.740
He expanded the little strength that illness left him, in preaching fidelity to the Orthodox

00:01:39.740 --> 00:01:46.820
faith, and to the Emperor, and in exhorting the people to have confidence in the aid of

00:01:46.820 --> 00:01:49.820
Saint Demetrios.

00:01:49.820 --> 00:01:58.100
During the Venetian occupation, in the years 1423 through 1430, he encouraged the people

00:01:58.100 --> 00:02:05.300
to bear with it, in order to delay the Turkish invasion for as long as possible.

00:02:05.300 --> 00:02:15.380
Six months before the city fell to Murad II, on the 29th of March in the year 1430, St. Simeon

00:02:15.380 --> 00:02:22.180
dreamt that he was in a richly decorated house, and heard a voice telling him not to

00:02:22.180 --> 00:02:31.460
tarry there, admiring its beauties, but to get out quickly before it fell to the ground.

00:02:31.460 --> 00:02:39.980
So he fell asleep in peace, spared the sad sight of the fall of his beloved city.

00:02:39.980 --> 00:02:46.860
The inhabitants of Thessalonica, whatever their race or religion, whether Orthodox, Latins

00:02:46.860 --> 00:02:55.580
or Jews, bewailed the loss of the father of them all, the good shepherd who had wholeheartedly

00:02:55.580 --> 00:02:59.940
given his life for his sheep.

00:02:59.940 --> 00:03:06.900
St. Simeon was one of the last disciples of St. Gregory Palamas, commemorated on the 14th

00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:14.100
of November, firmly established upon the rock of the faith, he clearly set forth Orthodox

00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:22.620
doctrine against every heresy, and illustrated it above all in his liturgical works.

00:03:22.620 --> 00:03:29.340
He brought to the conduct of divine service in the Church of St. Sophia in Thessalonica a

00:03:29.340 --> 00:03:35.140
splendor similar to that of the great church of Constantinople.

00:03:35.140 --> 00:03:43.300
He composed many hymns and prayers, and compiled a vast spiritual commentary on all the rights

00:03:43.300 --> 00:03:51.420
and ceremonies of the Byzantine Church, so that these treasures are not lost to us, even

00:03:51.420 --> 00:03:56.220
though the Christian Empire is no more.

00:03:56.220 --> 00:04:05.100
St. Simeon died more than 500 years ago, but it was not until the year 1981 that his veneration

00:04:05.580 --> 00:04:12.420
received the formal recognition of the ecumenical Patriarchate.

00:04:12.420 --> 00:04:18.580
Through the prayers of our Holy Father's, O Lord, Jesus Christ our God, have mercy on us

00:04:18.580 --> 00:04:19.660
and save us.
